      "message": "test(ui): the colour guard strips comments after code and joins theme_files\n\nReview of #3990: the guard skipped only lines that start with `//`. A\ncomment inside a call hid a literal (`from_rgb(1, // red` counted 0),\nand a colour in a comment after code counted 1. The scanner now\nremoves `//` and nested `/* */` comments and keeps the text of string\nand char literals. Tests pin the two review probes, a `//` in a string\nand in a raw string, a quote char literal, a lifetime, and a nested\nblock comment.\n\nThe guard moves into the theme_files suite (#3187: no new test binary).\nIts scanner is split into theme_files/colour_scan.rs (400-line law).\nThe theme_files gate map names ui::egui_app, so each UI change runs it.\n\nRefs #1120\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
